  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "OZHW6qq43pgiKdXGlbgUI1MQGvc=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:17.644Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Dutch arm of Sopra Steria is credited with the best framework access in the Netherlands and, in the same sentence, the weakest partnership fit in the set. Its recorded stack is Microsoft and Salesforce \u2014 proprietary alliances with no open-source anchor \u2014 and it sits at priority 9.\n\nThe two halves of that verdict are not independent. The reason a firm accumulates framework positions is that it has been an accepted large-scale supplier for years, and that same history is what builds deep alliances with the platform vendors government buyers already procure. The credentials that create access are the credentials that fill the slot.\n\nThis is why the screen ranks partnership fit above route-to-market. An inaccessible good partner can be helped into a framework, or reached through one that already has a position; a well-positioned firm with no reason to carry your layer cannot be argued into wanting it. Kainos shows the same inversion in the UK with evidenced framework coverage and Workday anchoring, and the UK Sopra Steria entity records it in almost identical words.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Sopra Steria Netherlands (NL)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Best NL framework access, weakest partnership fit.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:28:17.644060Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:17.644065Z"
    }
  },
